{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the complete S4 implementation at head 1e36fb120dec880d2e64cd5f1edeac81e7ffbaa2, tree 2ca3bb32, for request a7d77a9b as amended by 2c938074, and review request 92305611. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED.\n\nThe head adds 40 paths to main 112eff12. I read the note first, then all of `apps/views`, the MCP changes and the Brief profile. One independent read ran beside mine, and I confirmed each finding below in the code. I ran item 1's failure only through that read's scratch run, and items 2 and 3 come from reading the code, not from a run.\n\nThe design holds. No authority is widened, and the bounds, the local mark and the Brief all do what the note says. The defects are in how the new reads answer at their edges.\n\n## Changes requested\n\n1. A no-argument read is refused when the client omits `arguments`.\n   - `wire.ts:246` passes `params[\"arguments\"]`, `service.ts:384` hands it to `ApplicationReads.call` unchanged, and `read-tools.ts` requires a record.\n   - Scenario: `tools/call {name:\"needs_you\"}` returns `{error:\"application-read\",reason:\"shape\"}`. MCP allows that call, and `work` and `since` behave the same. Every other tool in this service defaults to `{}`.\n   - Fix: pass `given`, and add a case.\n\n2. A Question that changes before Approve gives a protocol error, not a stale card.\n   - `decision.ts` `admit` throws `Unread(\"question-changed\")`. `service.ts:572` awaits it without a catch, `views/tools.ts` rethrows anything that isn't a `ViewError`, `#failure` rethrows it, and `wire.ts` answers -32603 \"Internal error\". Any failed read during admission takes the same path.\n   - `session.ts` has already retained the rejected dispatch under that key, so a retry at the same cut repeats the error. No act is signed, so this fails closed.\n   - A revised Question is the ordinary case this check exists for, so the user needs the same stale answer that a declared view gives.\n   - Fix: throw `ViewError(\"stale\", ...)` from `admit`, or convert there, and add a case with a Question revised between display and Approve.\n\n3. `context` can attach a comment about another scope's fact.\n   - `matchItem` compares `value.seq` and ignores `value.at`. Line 346 of `repo-in-ai.ts` uses it for comments, and the comment's `about` is a FactRef.\n   - Scenario: in lane A, a member comments with `about` naming seq K in lane B, and lane A has a version or approval at seq K. The comment appears as being about that lane A entry, in a result marked `complete: true`.\n   - I read this path but did not run native acceptance of a foreign `about`. If the native rule refuses it, say so in the note and keep the check anyway, because this reader shouldn't depend on it.\n   - Fix: for a FactRef, also require `at` to equal the frame's scope. Add a case.\n\n4. The history count charges one entry twice, and its comment says something else.\n   - `Collection.entry` charges the `bodyAt` entry at `reads.ts:186-189`, and the history loop at `repo-in-ai.ts:328-330` charges it again. So a lane of exactly 50 entries is refused, against the stated limit of 50.\n   - The comment at line 323 says \"only actual question entries\", but the loop charges the whole lane from seq 0.\n   - Consequence: any Question in a lane of 50 entries or more has no `context` and no Decision card, permanently. That fails closed, and neither `docs/mcp.md` nor `apps/views/README.md` says it.\n   - Fix: charge each entry once, correct the comment, and state this consequence in both pages.\n\n5. The fallback for a large Question leads nowhere, and `context` returns more than it describes.\n   - The card refuses a body over its 60 KiB budget and says to read the bounded context. A legal body of 65,536 bytes appears in both `body` and `versions[].text`, and `result()` holds the value twice, so the answer passes `RESULT_BYTES` and returns `context-output-limit`.\n   - `context.items` also returns every live lane item with duplicates, including other Questions. The tool's description doesn't name them, and a moderately busy lane can reach the same limit.\n   - Fix: remove `items` from the public answer, and remove the repeated body. Add a case at the largest legal body.\n\n6. A stale mark reports the wrong reason.\n   - In `decision.ts`, a `ViewError` from `admit` falls into the last branch and becomes `local-review-write`, although nothing was written.\n   - Fix: return its own reason.\n\nItems 1 to 6 change production code or its tests, so one new full gate must run at the final source. Gate 3 stays a pass for its own source, and both earlier failed gates stay failed.\n\n## What holds\n\n- The six plan witnesses and the amendment's witness each have an assertion:\n  - another person's request stays out of the list;\n  - a met request leaves it;\n  - nine scopes leave one unread;\n  - the Brief digest equals the Question's pin;\n  - `since` is empty after a mark and then shows one new entry;\n  - every work row names a controller;\n  - `revise-ask` with a different Brief is refused with `brief-fixed`, in a native test.\n- Viewer binding: one active key, one active member, roster and Directory bound to each other, and the two Membership and two Directory pins named exactly. `ROLE_LISTS` uses `hasOwn`.\n- Bounds: scopes, pages, requests and items are charged before the work, and bytes are charged per chunk. The default fetch uses `redirect: \"error\"`, an abort and a deadline. The route and method allowlists hold. Omissions, unread scopes and clipped rows set `complete: false`.\n- The read floor: `handle.summary` checks the minimum, and held frames check it again.\n- The local mark: `checkedLocal` compares the capture with the displayed heads and ranges, heads are read again, and `admit` runs with no await before the rename. The review store's path, owner, mode, link, cap, rollback and conflict checks all hold. Its failure after the rename stops without a repeat.\n- The Brief: raw bytes through `digestBytes`, a strict UTF-8 round trip, one fixed URI and no loader. `issue-questions.ts` is unchanged.\n- The kernel filing gate: nothing under `packages/contract`, `bytes`, `derive`, `scope` or `platform` changes. The definition uses existing forms, as the note says, so the gate asks for nothing more. `check-kernel-boundary` checks 127 sources with 0 refusals.\n- The ordinary MCP service keeps its catalogue and its watch. The seals change only for `service.ts`.\n\n## Gate and checks at this head\n\n- The gate at 399269c7, tree 576a5010, closed 0/0 with complete capture, no dropped bytes and matching source after the run. Its `test.log` shows Node 91, Counting 56, Plain 3,202 with one skip and Native 889 with two skips.\n- From 399269c7 to this head, only the note and the manifest change.\n- The evidence verifies. All 253 cited unit files and 26 extras match. The seven collections have 593, 316, 250, 378, 138, 79 and 362 files, each `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean, and no file is writable.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 112eff12 gives tree 2ca3bb32. The remerge diff of 3fd9cc28 shows no hand change.\n- I ran these once each:\n  - `apps/views/test/s4.test.mjs` passes 7 of 7;\n  - `issue-questions-brief.scope.test.ts` passes 1 of 1;\n  - `security-entry-points.test.mjs` passes 10 of 10;\n  - `check-notes` gives 0 warnings;\n  - `check-commit-messages` checks 23 with 0 flagged;\n  - `check-doc-links` on an export finds 775 links with 0 broken;\n  - `git diff --check` is clean.\n- The worktree stayed clean.\n\n## For the planner\n\n1. Is a limit of 50 lane entries acceptable for the Decision card? An Issue lane with commitments, comments and revisions can reach it, and the Question then stays unavailable for good. Item 4 only makes the limit honest. Raising it, or reading fewer entries, is a design choice, and the S1 real-room render is the first place it could bite.\n2. A room with more than six lanes never offers Mark reviewed, because `since` is then never complete. The lanes are selected in a stable order, so the same ones stay omitted. The note says that a mark \"covers displayed heads, not omitted scopes\", but the code offers no mark when a scope is omitted. The code fails closed, so I ask only that the note match it. You may want a way to reach the omitted lanes.\n3. The request says that `since` shows each new head once. The head shows it once per response and repeats it until a mark, and `docs/mcp.md` says so. That is the pure read the plan's witness needs, and I read it as meeting the request. Rule otherwise if you meant something else.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The review store has one cap of 64 heads across every binding, with no way to clear it. A stale lock after a crash answers `busy` until someone removes it. Both fail closed.\n2. A Question with many separate texts can reach the 16-page limit, and that also fails closed.\n3. I did not recompute the Brief pin digest with `pin.mjs`, and neither read audited the non-S4 parts of `declared.ts`.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe local adapter stays outside the kernel, the catalogue is static and the Decision card uses the existing signing path. Approved, with the planner's question on the limit.\n\n## Security\n\nNo authority is added, a mark signs nothing, and neither read found a credential or markup path. Item 3 is a wrong attribution under `complete: true`, so it needs fixing. Item 2 fails closed but hides the reason. Changes requested, items 2 and 3.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe reads are compact and the local mark is small. Item 5 removes output nobody asked for. Approved, with item 5.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: changes requested, items 2 and 3.\n- Simplification: approved, with item 5.\n- The request's checks:\n  - These hold: the plan witnesses, the amendment, the filing gate and the evidence.\n  - These are needed: items 1 to 6, each with its case where named, and one full gate at the final source.\n\nA head that makes these changes can come back for a review of its diff from this head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:31d2e6ceed845119be775798009141b755e34934","binding":"assigned","head":"1e36fb120dec880d2e64cd5f1edeac81e7ffbaa2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:507223f4141c2c2c68fb5cbe102948baba26edd5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:185054c48cd88f847085bf417d43df15648e1f49\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b4144924e2ad5641d750789533418dd92854bb92","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0290ad7b6553feaaa6c037ba7c460441af409b2a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03af7c9c3f2499777dc7c314ab891b47b7e83644, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0bc5f13ba3f9a5e8d8db9da39edb8212a3a04937, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0fe26da8629348f9fa7d2b14c1eaa78d04e20872, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18a4df0817708d72468bffad53377fdf158b19c3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18b3c47c2325f8393faee58c4987799644a39632, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2491acbc1c7ca6358749971c79e51b71b1942360, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2d1edaf30405284874bea196e5cdeddb034d6d26, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:31d2e6ceed845119be775798009141b755e34934, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:33b88c4dc400ea443bda61ed14aa273b40b7203a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:434144e21b5e82e43b47b99a176c78c70b491517, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:494eac68d16b0dd36d3430b029d291b7f736ca27, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4ce6184dbbea257246b0dc3239cd7cce29f4c